Z||000000||Tobin01||07-10-2001||01:51 AM||||i have a 1990 454 truck engine and i wanna put it in a fiero but do i need a gt or can i put it in a 2m4?<BR>cuz its one hell of a big engine||||reg||1
Z||000001||pontiacs4me||07-10-2001||01:54 AM||||first of all welcome to the forum, second of all all fiero engine bays are the same size.  If you want to put a 454 in a fiero, it can be done, but good luck with cooling, and keeping the transmission alive.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||07-10-2001||02:00 AM||||A big block Chevy engine is not all that much bigger than a small block. I went through the same measurement stuff when I was measuring my Aerocoupe for a 454... it is just a few inches difference.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tobin01||07-10-2001||02:18 AM||||pontiacs4me<BR>i have an intercooler which should fit on the  in and i can try to put a scoop  on 1 but i dunno if itll work out rite||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrgone||07-10-2001||02:23 AM||||no trunklid = no cooling problem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">   <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pontiaddict||07-10-2001||04:10 AM||||A big block is 2 inches wider, 2 inches taller, and 2.5 inches longer than a small block. (give or take due to varying external parts like intake and exhaust manifolds) It's also 110 lbs heavier than a SBC.||||reg||1
Z||000006||KRMFiero||07-10-2001||06:48 AM||||If your going to use that engine (so you dont have pullys and stuff rubbing your tire) you will need to move the Transmitsion over more to the drivers side, I belive HTD sells stuff to move the Transmission: <A HREF="http://www.hi-techdev.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.hi-techdev.com/</A> <P>Personally if I was you I would cut your trunk out and Longatudaly mount it but that probley a b*tch to do<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000007||Boomtastic||07-10-2001||07:27 AM||||Gary Zumalt used to have a 454 in one of his Fieros. (I have it on video - not running - from Carlisle '93) I have his handout from the show at home, but I believe the company he worked with to sell it (Heritage A&F) has folded. If you want their (old) contact info, just let me know.||||reg||1
